---
import ContentGrid from "../../../components/UI/ContentGrid.astro";
---

<ContentGrid
  title="Progressive Quality Gates in CI/CD"
  description="I balanced the trade-off between <strong>catching critical issues early</strong> (preventing costly post-merge fixes) and <strong>maintaining development velocity</strong> by categorizing gates into tiers—reserving hard blocks only for violations that would directly impact user experience or create technical debt." 
  columns={3}
  items={[
    {
      icon: 'line-md:close-circle',
      iconColor: 'text-red-500',
      title: 'Tier 1: Must-Fix (Blocks PR)',
      content: [
        'Critical accessibility violations',
        'Design token violations in core',
        'Breaking changes to public APIs',
        'Bundle size budget exceeded'
      ]
    },
    {
      icon: 'line-md:alert',
      iconColor: 'text-orange-500',
      title: 'Tier 2: Should-Fix (Accept)',
      content: [
        'Medium-priority accessibility issues',
        'Performance warnings (not critical)',
        'Deprecated pattern usage',
        '"Acknowledge & Merge" w/ explanation'
      ]
    },
    {
      icon: 'line-md:lightbulb',
      iconColor: 'text-blue-500',
      title: 'Tier 3: Nice-to-Fix (Inform)',
      content: [
        'Minor best practice suggestions',
        'Performance optimization opportunities',
        'Does not block merge',
        'Can add contextual hints'
      ]
    }
  ]}
/>

<div class="card p-6 mt-6">
  <h4 class="font-semibold mb-1">How I Set These Tiers</h4>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-4 dark:text-gray-400">I worked with frontend leads, accessibility team, and product to define criteria. We experimented: started with fewer hard gates, gradually tightened based on data. Tracked which warnings got ignored → promoted to hard gates if critical.</p>

  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-400">
    <div class="bg-gray-100 rounded p-3 dark:bg-black/20">
      <div class="font-semibold mb-1 dark:text-gray-200">Result:</div>
      <div class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-400">53% fewer review cycles (3.2 → 1.5 avg per PR)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-gray-100 rounded p-3 dark:bg-black/20">
      <div class="font-semibold mb-1 dark:text-gray-200">Quality:</div>
      <div class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-400">No critical accessibility violations merged</div>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-gray-100 rounded p-3 dark:bg-black/20">
      <div class="font-semibold mb-1 dark:text-gray-200">Adoption:</div>
      <div class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-400">90% of PRs passed quality gates on first try</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
